WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.533
I've called till my throat bleeds.

00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:00.833
Is there no man among you?

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.900
That garden you all weep for.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.933
That paradise.

00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:20.333
Which of you do I send to it first?

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:22.433
MECCA · Eleven Years Earlier

00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:24.433
A strong one! Young!

00:03:24.433 --> 00:03:27.833
Good teeth, a back for any load! Who gives ten?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.033
Eight? Then eight, for a back like this!

00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:34.033
Sold!

00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:48.066
Eight, for a grown man? I've paid more for a goat.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.366
Then buy him. A year this cheap doesn't come twice.

00:04:59.433 --> 00:05:01.166
Peace on this house, Uncle.

00:05:05.266 --> 00:05:08.500
Ali. Come — come here, boy. Sit.

00:05:11.733 --> 00:05:14.600
Water for him. And the dates, the soft ones.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.366
Does your father not feed you?

00:05:30.166 --> 00:05:33.200
How is Abu Talib? His chest, in the mornings —

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.433
is it still bad?

00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:50.400
So. What brings my brother's son to my door

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.633
with the road still on his feet,

00:05:51.633 --> 00:05:52.433
hm?

00:05:52.766 --> 00:05:54.433
The son of Abdullah, Muhammad,

00:05:54.466 --> 00:05:56.366
asks the family to his house tonight.

00:05:56.466 --> 00:05:58.233
And he asks that no one is missing.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.233
He sends you.

00:06:05.533 --> 00:06:06.933
My brother's son.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.066
Around the whole of Mecca.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.833
Like a water-boy, to carry his invitations

00:06:11.833 --> 00:06:13.066
and fill his room.

00:06:13.733 --> 00:06:16.033
When a man wants Abd al-Uzza at his table,

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:19.200
he comes to my door on his own two feet, and he asks me himself.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.633
He does not send a child with a basket.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.600
Abd al-Uzza has sat at better tables

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.466
than a widow's son can set.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.966
You're a good boy, Ali. Finish the water.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.700
And take that back to the one who sent you.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.166
Ali. Son of Abu Talib.

00:07:37.033 --> 00:07:39.433
What brings you to my door, son?

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:50.066
My cousin, the son of Abdullah, Muhammad,

00:07:50.366 --> 00:07:52.033
invites you to his house tonight.

00:07:55.733 --> 00:07:57.333
Abu Talib's house has started

00:07:57.333 --> 00:08:00.433
summoning its elders through the mouths of children. Boy.

00:08:01.133 --> 00:08:03.300
Carry this back the way you carried it in.

00:08:04.266 --> 00:08:06.166
A man who wants me at his table

00:08:06.166 --> 00:08:08.500
brings the invitation on his own two feet.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:10.166
Not through children.

00:08:25.933 --> 00:08:27.933
…on his own two feet…

00:08:36.733 --> 00:08:39.466
…a man who wants me at his table…

00:08:47.666 --> 00:08:50.066
…he does not send a child…

00:08:55.733 --> 00:08:56.966
…not through children…

00:09:14.466 --> 00:09:17.133
I carried it to all of them, Messenger of Allah.

00:09:18.266 --> 00:09:21.800
The far houses, the poor ones — they'll come.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.200
But the great men… they all said the one thing.

00:09:25.633 --> 00:09:27.500
That a man who wants them at his table

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.633
should come to them himself.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.633
On his own two feet.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.200
Not through a boy.

00:09:44.733 --> 00:09:46.200
Should I go with you?

00:11:33.633 --> 00:11:35.866
Is this why you called us to your house?

00:11:36.166 --> 00:11:39.166
To fill our stomachs — and then set our own blood

00:11:39.166 --> 00:11:41.433
against the gods our fathers died under?

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.066
He would put down Lat. Uzza.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.766
The trade that feeds every child in this room.

00:11:46.766 --> 00:11:48.600
Everything this valley was built on —

00:11:48.933 --> 00:11:52.433
for words he carried back out of a cave. Alone.

00:11:57.033 --> 00:11:59.500
So. Which of you.

00:12:00.133 --> 00:12:04.133
Which of you will stand at his side, against every tribe

00:12:04.133 --> 00:12:05.433
from here to Sham,

00:12:05.566 --> 00:12:07.433
against your own fathers in the ground?

00:12:08.033 --> 00:12:09.000
Say it.

00:12:09.666 --> 00:12:11.366
Let me hear one voice.

00:12:20.633 --> 00:12:22.200
Not one of you.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.266
Say it.

00:12:26.366 --> 00:12:27.366
I will.

00:12:44.166 --> 00:12:46.100
I will, Messenger of Allah.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.366
I am the youngest in this house.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.700
My eyes are weak, my arms are thin —

00:12:53.766 --> 00:12:55.566
you have all seen it with your own eyes.

00:12:56.033 --> 00:12:59.266
But not one man here has caught him in a lie in forty

00:12:59.266 --> 00:13:00.100
years.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.333
Not one of you.

00:13:06.766 --> 00:13:09.633
I will not stand in his house and call him a liar

00:13:09.633 --> 00:13:11.266
by keeping my mouth shut.

00:13:12.866 --> 00:13:15.500
If the whole of Mecca stands against you —

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.466
I am still here.

00:13:25.433 --> 00:13:27.866
It has come to this in your house, Abu Talib.

00:13:28.433 --> 00:13:32.266
A boy speaks — and the men of Hashim swallow their tongues.

00:14:02.966 --> 00:14:06.700
Grow up small and quiet, boy. It suits you.

00:15:02.966 --> 00:15:04.033
A child.

00:15:04.733 --> 00:15:06.733
Forty men of Hashim in that room —

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.100
and the one who stood for him was a child.

00:15:10.033 --> 00:15:11.133
Sit, Abu Lahab.

00:15:11.566 --> 00:15:13.866
You've walked the whole way here carrying it.

00:15:17.233 --> 00:15:21.033
They laughed. In my own brother's house.

00:15:23.566 --> 00:15:25.633
By morning the whole valley has it.

00:15:28.733 --> 00:15:31.833
A boy stood up. Let them laugh at the boy.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:33.500
That is not the thing

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.733
that should keep a chief of Quraysh awake at night.

00:15:35.733 --> 00:15:37.200
Then say what should.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:46.300
How many go to him now, in the nights?

00:15:53.133 --> 00:15:54.633
Count them for me.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:16:01.800
The poor. Slaves. A few of the young. Nothing.
— Nothing.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.700
Yesterday it was nothing.

00:16:07.033 --> 00:16:10.100
Today it is your own brother's blood, on his feet

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:11.700
in a room full of chiefs.

00:16:21.933 --> 00:16:24.766
Hamza acted in temper. He'll cool.

00:16:24.766 --> 00:16:26.433
And the one after Hamza?

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:29.666
A man with a sword, who does not cool?

00:16:35.266 --> 00:16:37.066
You put a thing out while it is small,

00:16:37.066 --> 00:16:40.100
Abu Lahab. Not when it is already in your roof.

00:16:42.933 --> 00:16:45.466
Then we put it out. Tonight.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.800
A knife in the dark, and it is finished.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.133
And by morning, every man who half-listened to him

00:16:57.133 --> 00:16:58.900
weeps for a murdered saint.

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:05.366
His uncle shields him.

00:17:06.033 --> 00:17:07.100
Put a knife in him,

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:08.933
and you open a war with half of Hashim

00:17:08.933 --> 00:17:11.133
over a man they still call the truthful one.

00:17:19.833 --> 00:17:20.200
So.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:24.000
The great Amr ibn Hisham tells me to sit on my hands.

00:17:26.566 --> 00:17:29.866
I said you do not knife a man you can first make small.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.400
This House is my blood's House.

00:17:36.966 --> 00:17:39.400
Do not lecture me on what it is worth.

00:17:39.566 --> 00:17:40.800
Then you know it.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.233
Every tribe in Arabia comes to these stones.

00:17:44.366 --> 00:17:46.733
To the gods in them. Through our roads,

00:17:46.733 --> 00:17:47.800
at our price.

00:17:48.433 --> 00:17:49.866
That is our silver.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.433
That is why a Qurayshi's word is heard

00:17:52.433 --> 00:17:53.633
from here to Sham.

00:17:55.666 --> 00:17:57.333
And he would empty it.

00:17:58.666 --> 00:17:59.766
For a god?

00:18:00.566 --> 00:18:03.233
No man gathers the poor and the hungry around himself

00:18:03.233 --> 00:18:05.233
for a god. He gathers them

00:18:05.233 --> 00:18:06.766
because a man with a crowd at his back

00:18:06.766 --> 00:18:08.466
takes what other men are holding.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:15.933
He wants Mecca.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:18.333
He wants what you and I hold.

00:18:18.733 --> 00:18:20.866
The House. The road.

00:18:21.566 --> 00:18:23.433
Men who go quiet when he speaks.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.766
Then that is what Mecca hears.

00:18:31.066 --> 00:18:32.200
Before he ever stands

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.900
and calls himself sent down from the sky —

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:35.133
you stand first.

00:18:35.133 --> 00:18:37.533
And you tell them what he is truly reaching for.

00:18:37.533 --> 00:18:39.766
Their House. Their trade.

00:18:40.133 --> 00:18:41.100
Their necks.

00:18:41.933 --> 00:18:43.100
Not a prophet.

00:18:43.866 --> 00:18:46.100
A man who means to sit above them.

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.400
And they hear it from his own blood.

00:18:50.533 --> 00:18:52.033
That is why it holds.

00:19:01.133 --> 00:19:03.466
Tomorrow. On the steps.

00:19:42.366 --> 00:19:45.066
Gather! Gather at the House!

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:47.233
A chief of Quraysh will speak!

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:26.900
People of Mecca! Sons of Quraysh!

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:33.666
Hear me — because

00:20:33.666 --> 00:20:36.433
I did not come out this morning against one man.

00:20:36.866 --> 00:20:38.466
Or one man's words.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:40.766
I came out for everything

00:20:40.766 --> 00:20:43.800
the men before us raised with their own hands,

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.800
and left in ours to keep.

00:20:48.633 --> 00:20:51.633
You were all born in the shade of this House.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:55.266
Around these stones your fathers set their trade,

00:20:55.333 --> 00:20:59.033
their name, their blood. And it has stood.

00:21:02.266 --> 00:21:05.100
Did Lat not give us our standing among the tribes?

00:21:05.266 --> 00:21:07.500
Did Uzza not fill your caravans?

00:21:07.766 --> 00:21:11.166
Did the gods of this House not make Mecca the one city

00:21:11.166 --> 00:21:13.333
all of Arabia must come to?

00:21:18.233 --> 00:21:20.033
And now a man of my own blood

00:21:20.033 --> 00:21:22.266
tells you to throw all of it in the dust.

00:21:25.333 --> 00:21:27.400
He tells the slave you bought yesterday —

00:21:27.666 --> 00:21:29.433
the one who lowers his eyes when you pass —

00:21:29.433 --> 00:21:31.733
that he carries the same soul as his master.

00:21:31.733 --> 00:21:35.000
That he should sit at your table. As your equal.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:53.133
No city stands on that. Your slaves. Your women.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:58.200
What your fathers willed to you. Who speaks,

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.300
and who stays silent.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:03.500
He would turn every part of it over.

00:22:08.933 --> 00:22:11.633
And do not let him tell you it is for a god.

00:22:14.133 --> 00:22:16.033
No man gathers the poor,

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:19.366
and the hungry, and the desperate around himself

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.433
for a god. He gathers them

00:22:21.433 --> 00:22:23.566
because a man with a crowd at his back

00:22:23.566 --> 00:22:25.566
reaches for what other men are holding.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:28.900
He does not come to serve you, people of Mecca.

00:22:29.366 --> 00:22:31.433
He comes to sit above you.

00:22:31.600 --> 00:22:34.633
Not a messenger — a master.

00:22:40.333 --> 00:22:43.100
Not while I stand on these steps.

00:22:50.233 --> 00:22:52.500
Whoever opens his door to this —

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:56.666
whoever gives it bread, or a roof, or one night's shelter —

00:22:56.666 --> 00:23:01.100
answers to me. And to every man of Quraysh standing here.

00:23:01.566 --> 00:23:06.500
Let his own two hands be the ones that bury him.

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:15.500
You've been sitting there since you came in,

00:24:15.533 --> 00:24:18.133
turning something over in your hands that isn't there.

00:24:20.366 --> 00:24:21.833
It's nothing, Father.

00:24:23.533 --> 00:24:26.800
It has kept your eyes on the floor since dusk.

00:24:32.066 --> 00:24:33.500
That is not nothing.

00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:39.533
Uncle Abu Lahab stood on the steps of the House

00:24:39.533 --> 00:24:40.433
this morning.

00:24:41.033 --> 00:24:42.700
In front of all of Mecca.

00:24:45.266 --> 00:24:47.000
I heard what he said.

00:24:48.633 --> 00:24:51.200
The whole valley heard it by midday.

00:24:51.266 --> 00:24:52.833
He didn't say he was wrong.

00:24:53.100 --> 00:24:54.800
He didn't argue with him at all.

00:24:55.300 --> 00:24:58.533
He called him a danger. A man reaching for the city.

00:25:01.933 --> 00:25:03.800
That's worse than calling him a liar.

00:25:04.666 --> 00:25:07.566
A liar, you answer. This—

00:25:12.533 --> 00:25:14.900
This, they act on.

00:25:17.933 --> 00:25:18.933
Yes.

00:25:23.433 --> 00:25:25.133
I stood up in a room, Father.

00:25:25.233 --> 00:25:27.566
That's all I did. Stand up.

00:25:27.566 --> 00:25:27.966
And now

00:25:27.966 --> 00:25:30.100
his own family has turned the whole city against him,

00:25:30.100 --> 00:25:30.900
and I—

00:25:34.766 --> 00:25:37.400
I don't know what a boy is supposed to do with that.

00:25:40.266 --> 00:25:42.133
Tonight? Nothing.

00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:44.833
You do nothing tonight.

00:25:48.233 --> 00:25:49.066
Nothing—

00:25:49.266 --> 00:25:51.833
A fire is not put out the night it is lit.

00:25:52.466 --> 00:25:55.633
Not by a man. Not by a boy.

00:26:02.366 --> 00:26:03.166
You look at me

00:26:03.166 --> 00:26:06.033
as if I have to decide whether to stand behind him.

00:26:06.800 --> 00:26:09.300
I decided that long before you were born.

00:26:16.866 --> 00:26:18.066
When my father died,

00:26:18.066 --> 00:26:20.633
he left me a boy to raise who was not my son.

00:26:20.966 --> 00:26:23.100
No mother. No father.

00:26:23.166 --> 00:26:27.000
Nothing to his name. And I had little enough for my own.

00:26:29.666 --> 00:26:31.600
In all the years he sat at my fire,

00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:33.566
I never once caught him in a lie.

00:26:33.766 --> 00:26:36.166
Not as a child. Not as a man.

00:26:37.333 --> 00:26:40.400
So do not ask me whether I can hold back from him now.

00:26:43.333 --> 00:26:46.166
A man does not weigh a debt like that on a scale.

00:26:49.766 --> 00:26:51.733
Do you know why I named you Ali?

00:26:53.333 --> 00:26:56.266
Mother called me Haydar. The lion.

00:26:57.666 --> 00:26:58.666
She did.

00:26:59.600 --> 00:27:02.300
She saw a thing in you that does not lie down.

00:27:04.366 --> 00:27:06.033
And I called you Ali.

00:27:06.633 --> 00:27:07.866
The high one.

00:27:08.566 --> 00:27:10.566
Not to stand over other men.

00:27:11.366 --> 00:27:13.166
So that your head never goes down

00:27:13.166 --> 00:27:14.400
where it should not go.

00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:16.966
No hand reaches you, or him,

00:27:16.966 --> 00:27:18.900
while I stand between you and it.

00:27:19.033 --> 00:27:21.333
Not his enemies. Not mine.

00:27:29.066 --> 00:27:30.066
So.

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:33.500
What does a boy do tonight, with all of it?

00:27:34.033 --> 00:27:37.066
He keeps his eyes up. And he sleeps.

00:27:38.500 --> 00:27:40.566
Tomorrow is soon enough to be a lion.

00:28:31.966 --> 00:28:34.166
Go back. Take another step,

00:28:34.166 --> 00:28:36.133
and I swear you will walk home alone.

00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:56.866
Where are you taking her?

00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:02.433
This doesn't concern you, traveler.

00:29:04.200 --> 00:29:06.933
She's mine to answer for. Go on your way.

00:29:10.533 --> 00:29:13.400
A man only says that when he already knows the answer

00:29:13.400 --> 00:29:14.466
would shame him.

00:29:17.200 --> 00:29:19.133
You don't know what it is to be shamed.

00:29:19.966 --> 00:29:21.733
To have men look at your sons and count

00:29:21.733 --> 00:29:24.733
only daughters. To carry that name through the market

00:29:24.733 --> 00:29:25.966
every day of your life.

00:29:25.966 --> 00:29:28.266
I know what you'll call it on the way out there.

00:29:28.566 --> 00:29:30.600
Honor. The tribe.

00:29:30.766 --> 00:29:33.833
What your father did, and his father before him.

00:29:36.500 --> 00:29:39.333
Every man who has ever walked a child into that desert

00:29:39.333 --> 00:29:41.833
called it something clean before he reached the end.

00:29:43.966 --> 00:29:45.233
It is honor.

00:29:57.633 --> 00:30:02.100
Baba… you're holding my hand too tight. It hurts.

00:30:07.266 --> 00:30:07.866
One day,

00:30:07.866 --> 00:30:10.566
everything buried will be dug up and made to speak.

00:30:10.733 --> 00:30:14.033
The sky. The seas. The stars.

00:30:16.466 --> 00:30:18.333
And on that day it is not the fathers

00:30:18.333 --> 00:30:21.266
who will be asked to explain themselves. It is her.

00:30:23.233 --> 00:30:26.933
They will turn to her, with the sand still in her mouth,

00:30:27.133 --> 00:30:29.300
and ask what she did to deserve it.

00:30:29.966 --> 00:30:31.866
What will you have her say?

00:31:13.066 --> 00:31:15.300
You've been somewhere else all evening.

00:31:20.066 --> 00:31:22.366
I saw a man on the road today.

00:31:23.733 --> 00:31:24.700
…And?

00:31:27.833 --> 00:31:30.333
A free man. Good cloak.

00:31:31.100 --> 00:31:33.900
The kind who steps around people like us in the market.

00:31:35.933 --> 00:31:39.066
He stopped in the open road for a girl who wasn't his.

00:31:39.533 --> 00:31:42.066
A daughter, being taken out to be buried.

00:31:49.033 --> 00:31:50.333
Men do that.

00:31:50.900 --> 00:31:52.466
It's not a new thing.

00:31:59.166 --> 00:32:00.800
He didn't shrug at it, Ammar.

00:32:01.566 --> 00:32:03.700
He stood in front of a man twice his weight,

00:32:03.766 --> 00:32:05.666
over a child that would never carry his name,

00:32:05.666 --> 00:32:07.366
that could never pay him back a single coin…

00:32:07.366 --> 00:32:11.000
and he argued for her. Like she was worth something.

00:32:17.366 --> 00:32:19.966
One of them. One of Muhammad's.

00:32:21.633 --> 00:32:23.000
I didn't ask him.

00:32:23.633 --> 00:32:24.900
I didn't have to.

00:32:31.033 --> 00:32:32.700
Do you know what they'd do to us

00:32:32.766 --> 00:32:34.133
if they even thought we sat

00:32:34.133 --> 00:32:35.766
here, saying his name in the dark?

00:32:35.800 --> 00:32:38.133
I know exactly what they'd do to us.

00:32:38.866 --> 00:32:41.133
I've known what they can do to me my whole life,

00:32:41.133 --> 00:32:41.933
Ammar.

00:32:42.466 --> 00:32:44.133
That never needed a reason.

00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:48.400
This is the first time in my life

00:32:48.400 --> 00:32:49.866
I've heard there might be a reason

00:32:49.866 --> 00:32:51.033
for the other thing.

00:32:52.166 --> 00:32:53.500
What other thing?

00:32:55.566 --> 00:32:59.533
That a man like me, and a girl in that pit,

00:32:59.966 --> 00:33:01.933
and the one who owns us both —

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:04.266
that we might all stand the same.

00:33:04.800 --> 00:33:06.566
In front of the same One.

00:33:13.200 --> 00:33:16.866
Say it again. The part about standing the same.

00:33:40.700 --> 00:33:43.200
How many in this room still call it nothing?

00:33:44.200 --> 00:33:46.166
Huh. It is nothing.

00:33:46.333 --> 00:33:49.833
A handful of the poor, chasing a free meal and a story.

00:33:55.900 --> 00:33:57.000
A handful.

00:33:59.533 --> 00:34:01.600
Last season it was ten men.

00:34:01.866 --> 00:34:03.166
Now it is forty.

00:34:03.866 --> 00:34:06.600
And forty men who talk make eighty.

00:34:08.766 --> 00:34:11.666
You do not measure a fire by its size tonight.

00:34:12.100 --> 00:34:13.900
You measure it by how fast it took

00:34:13.900 --> 00:34:15.033
the last house.

00:34:16.133 --> 00:34:18.166
Then let his uncle deal with it.

00:34:18.600 --> 00:34:21.366
Abu Talib set this loose in his own family.

00:34:21.666 --> 00:34:22.666
Let him leash it.

00:34:25.200 --> 00:34:27.033
Abu Talib is one man.

00:34:27.566 --> 00:34:30.400
And one man's shadow only stretches so far.

00:34:30.800 --> 00:34:32.533
Everything standing inside it —

00:34:32.533 --> 00:34:34.133
his blood, his clan —

00:34:34.133 --> 00:34:36.666
we cannot touch, and you all know why.

00:34:39.100 --> 00:34:40.900
So we do not reach into the shadow.

00:34:41.300 --> 00:34:44.033
— Then who?
— The ones standing in the sun.

00:34:44.266 --> 00:34:45.733
No name, no clan,

00:34:45.733 --> 00:34:48.000
no father to come asking after the body.

00:34:48.100 --> 00:34:50.566
The slaves. The strangers.

00:34:51.133 --> 00:34:52.400
The bought men.

00:35:04.700 --> 00:35:08.633
Umar. Sit. You've come at the right hour.

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:11.566
We were just deciding where to begin.

00:35:12.233 --> 00:35:14.333
With the ones who have no one behind them.

00:35:18.033 --> 00:35:19.700
The slaves, you mean.

00:35:26.800 --> 00:35:30.233
Let me be sure I have understood the great men of Quraysh.

00:35:30.833 --> 00:35:33.166
You've sat in this room, all of you,

00:35:33.166 --> 00:35:37.100
and settled on a war. Against slaves.

00:35:38.100 --> 00:35:39.666
Against chained men.

00:35:41.033 --> 00:35:42.666
— Umar—
— The man you are afraid of

00:35:42.666 --> 00:35:45.500
stands in the open square every single day.

00:35:45.866 --> 00:35:48.766
He calls to your faces. He does not hide.

00:35:49.133 --> 00:35:51.633
And your answer is to go home and beat the people

00:35:51.633 --> 00:35:54.033
who cannot lift a hand to answer you.

00:35:57.033 --> 00:35:58.566
If Muhammad is a problem,

00:35:58.566 --> 00:36:00.966
he stands in the open square every day —

00:36:00.966 --> 00:36:02.666
go and face him like men.

00:36:04.600 --> 00:36:07.133
Don't tell me Quraysh has grown so weak

00:36:07.133 --> 00:36:09.733
it fights the people who can't fight back.

00:36:12.333 --> 00:36:13.966
You want to go at the man.

00:36:14.366 --> 00:36:15.900
I know you do, Umar.

00:36:17.466 --> 00:36:19.533
But the man has Hashim at his back,

00:36:19.533 --> 00:36:21.833
and his uncle's word over all of it.

00:36:23.900 --> 00:36:26.766
Put a hand on him today, and you do not kill a preacher —

00:36:26.766 --> 00:36:29.066
you start a blood-war among the clans,

00:36:29.533 --> 00:36:33.100
and hand him a grave the whole city will weep at.

00:36:34.266 --> 00:36:36.100
I am not looking for glory.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:39.866
Let the strong watch what happens to the weak —

00:36:40.066 --> 00:36:42.466
and the strong lose their taste for it.

00:36:43.766 --> 00:36:46.433
You just break the two or three no one will miss.

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:56.233
And charity begins in a man's own house, Umayyah.

00:36:57.566 --> 00:37:00.333
They tell me one of yours has already joined them.

00:37:05.433 --> 00:37:06.300
A lie.

00:37:06.400 --> 00:37:08.533
What I own follows what I follow.

00:37:08.666 --> 00:37:10.866
A slave has no religion but his master's.

00:37:17.800 --> 00:37:20.100
Then it will cost you nothing to prove it.

00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:23.500
Find the one who forgot that,

00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:27.866
and remind him, in front of the others, what a slave is.

00:37:32.533 --> 00:37:33.966
This city has an order.

00:37:34.333 --> 00:37:35.566
Our fathers built it,

00:37:35.566 --> 00:37:37.700
and every coin in Arabia still passes through it

00:37:37.700 --> 00:37:40.900
because it holds. I will not let one man empty the House

00:37:40.900 --> 00:37:43.633
our grandfathers filled. Not for a slave.

00:37:43.766 --> 00:37:46.666
Not for a stranger. Not for anyone.

00:38:32.666 --> 00:38:35.333
You've been with this house a long time, Bilal.

00:38:38.800 --> 00:38:40.066
Yes, master.

00:38:45.166 --> 00:38:46.766
A long time.

00:39:11.366 --> 00:39:12.533
Take this.

00:39:13.100 --> 00:39:14.633
Set it before the god.

00:39:19.700 --> 00:39:20.733
And bow.

00:39:40.600 --> 00:39:42.300
I set it down, master.

00:39:44.466 --> 00:39:46.666
I'll carry your water and your loads

00:39:46.900 --> 00:39:48.266
till my back breaks.

00:39:49.900 --> 00:39:52.700
But I won't put my head to the ground for a stone.

00:39:57.966 --> 00:40:01.233
I know. I know. You traitor.

00:40:03.066 --> 00:40:04.800
Say that again, you traitor.

00:40:05.466 --> 00:40:08.400
Look at where you are, and who is speaking to you,

00:40:08.400 --> 00:40:09.733
and say it again.

00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:15.766
I know where I am, master.

00:40:16.500 --> 00:40:18.200
And I know who I am.

00:40:22.566 --> 00:40:24.233
For the first time,

00:40:25.000 --> 00:40:26.766
I know who I am.

00:40:35.766 --> 00:40:37.566
You know who you are?

00:40:42.466 --> 00:40:44.466
I'll tell you who you are!

00:40:51.066 --> 00:40:53.466
You are a coin I spent!

00:40:55.533 --> 00:40:58.400
A back I bought to carry my loads!

00:41:03.866 --> 00:41:06.866
A self. A slave with a self.

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.666
Who put that in your mouth?

00:41:08.900 --> 00:41:11.600
Was it him? Was it Muhammad?

00:41:17.333 --> 00:41:20.633
Get him up. Out — into the street!

00:41:20.866 --> 00:41:23.366
Let the whole city see what I do with a slave

00:41:23.366 --> 00:41:25.066
who forgets his master!

00:41:44.133 --> 00:41:47.433
What did he do? He's Umayyah's water-carrier.

00:41:47.666 --> 00:41:51.566
He spat on the gods. Look at him. Watch what it buys.

00:42:29.666 --> 00:42:31.366
Every one of you knows me.

00:42:31.600 --> 00:42:35.066
You've traded at my door. You've borrowed on my word.

00:42:35.533 --> 00:42:37.933
And this one — you know him too.

00:42:38.233 --> 00:42:41.166
He carried your grain up from my stores on that back.

00:42:41.233 --> 00:42:44.933
Today he stood in my own courtyard. Looked me in the eye.

00:42:45.033 --> 00:42:47.400
And told me he would not bow to the gods

00:42:47.400 --> 00:42:48.900
your fathers bowed to.

00:42:50.266 --> 00:42:52.366
So understand what you are looking at.

00:42:52.766 --> 00:42:54.633
This is not one broken man.

00:42:54.700 --> 00:42:55.933
This is the sickness

00:42:55.933 --> 00:42:58.366
Hashim's dreamer is spreading through this city —

00:42:58.400 --> 00:43:00.400
the poison that tells the bought man

00:43:00.400 --> 00:43:02.733
he is your equal, and the servant

00:43:02.733 --> 00:43:05.000
he may lift his eyes to his master.

00:43:06.466 --> 00:43:09.166
Let it in, and there is no Mecca.

00:43:09.500 --> 00:43:11.333
There is a market with no order,

00:43:11.333 --> 00:43:13.866
and a house with no master.

00:43:13.866 --> 00:43:16.500
Name the gods. Curse his name.

00:43:17.666 --> 00:43:20.000
Or be as stubborn as your new god.

00:44:10.266 --> 00:44:13.466
It split in the night. On its own.

00:44:14.166 --> 00:44:16.966
A house's god does not crack on its own, Rabah.

00:44:17.700 --> 00:44:20.800
Not unless the house has done something to shame it.

00:44:24.600 --> 00:44:26.700
I'll go to the craftsman this morning, my lady.

00:44:26.866 --> 00:44:28.166
Before the market fills.

00:44:28.566 --> 00:44:31.900
Take coin for the best he has. Not the cheap stone —

00:44:32.166 --> 00:44:33.333
the good marble.

00:44:35.966 --> 00:44:37.100
I'll go with him.

00:44:39.600 --> 00:44:40.500
You?

00:44:44.100 --> 00:44:47.300
Mus'ab. The streets are ugly just now.

00:44:47.600 --> 00:44:50.266
There is a man of Hashim tearing this city in half,

00:44:50.266 --> 00:44:51.300
and men are being dragged

00:44:51.300 --> 00:44:53.500
through the market for standing too near him.

00:44:54.800 --> 00:44:57.700
You are the name this family has spent three generations

00:44:57.700 --> 00:44:58.500
building.

00:44:58.633 --> 00:45:01.733
Wherever you walk today, you walk as the son of Umayr.

00:45:02.000 --> 00:45:04.600
Don't let me hear your name anywhere near theirs.

00:45:06.633 --> 00:45:09.633
It's an errand for a stone, Mother. Nothing more.

00:45:49.866 --> 00:45:53.900
The house of Umayr — in my own workshop! Rabah,

00:45:53.966 --> 00:45:55.266
you should have sent word.

00:45:55.266 --> 00:45:57.766
I'd have carried the finest pieces to the door myself.

00:45:58.433 --> 00:46:00.666
One does not make the son of Umayr

00:46:00.666 --> 00:46:01.966
walk to a workshop.

00:46:02.266 --> 00:46:03.866
The lady's god cracked.

00:46:04.400 --> 00:46:06.466
She wants a replacement.
— Of course —

00:46:06.466 --> 00:46:09.800
of course. Only the best, for that house.

00:46:11.966 --> 00:46:14.200
Look at this one. Yemeni marble.

00:46:14.366 --> 00:46:17.166
Eleven days, this took me. Feel the face —

00:46:17.366 --> 00:46:19.533
the mouth, the set of the eyes.

00:46:19.600 --> 00:46:22.566
That is a god with dignity. Not some roadside stone.

00:46:28.600 --> 00:46:30.566
And when you buy from me, young master,

00:46:30.666 --> 00:46:33.866
you buy more than the stone. Anything happens to him —

00:46:33.866 --> 00:46:36.400
a crack, a chip, the colour fades in the sun —

00:46:36.400 --> 00:46:37.766
you bring him back to me.

00:46:37.766 --> 00:46:40.566
I mend the gods of the best houses in Mecca,

00:46:40.566 --> 00:46:43.000
free, for as long as they stand.

00:46:43.300 --> 00:46:45.466
Your grandfather bought from my father.

00:46:49.266 --> 00:46:53.266
You mend them.
— Better than new. Every time.

00:46:53.466 --> 00:46:56.100
A god you carry back to the man who made him

00:46:56.533 --> 00:46:57.633
when he breaks.

00:46:58.800 --> 00:47:00.733
Who else would mend him, master?

00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:04.166
I know where every seam is. I made him.

00:47:14.166 --> 00:47:16.966
Take the marble one, Rabah. She'll want the best.

00:47:42.033 --> 00:47:44.266
I watched a man make you.

00:47:51.200 --> 00:47:54.500
So tell me. On the day a man comes to break you,

00:47:54.500 --> 00:47:55.500
who do you call?

00:47:56.466 --> 00:47:59.400
Do you call him? The one with the chisel?

00:48:05.800 --> 00:48:07.066
…he tells the slave

00:48:07.066 --> 00:48:09.833
he carries the same soul as his master…

00:48:11.600 --> 00:48:14.433
…a house's god does not crack on its own…

00:48:16.666 --> 00:48:18.966
…I know where every seam is.

00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:22.033
I made him…
…not a messenger —

00:48:22.300 --> 00:48:23.433
a master…

00:48:23.933 --> 00:48:26.833
…don't let me hear your name anywhere near theirs…

00:48:30.700 --> 00:48:33.433
You cannot lift the hand he carved for you.

00:48:34.333 --> 00:48:37.133
You cannot turn the head he set on your shoulders.

00:48:39.733 --> 00:48:41.900
If I left you in the street tonight,

00:48:42.533 --> 00:48:44.400
you could not follow me home.

00:48:46.933 --> 00:48:48.733
What have I been kneeling to…

00:48:49.000 --> 00:48:50.766
that cannot stand on its own?

00:48:55.300 --> 00:48:56.833
If there is something in you —

00:48:56.833 --> 00:48:58.633
anything — move.

00:49:02.933 --> 00:49:04.133
Say something.

00:49:48.166 --> 00:49:51.200
You looked at me. In my own house.

00:49:51.300 --> 00:49:53.000
In front of my own servants.

00:49:53.233 --> 00:49:57.166
A thing I paid for — lifting its eyes to me.

00:50:02.266 --> 00:50:04.566
You'll undo it where they can all see.

00:50:04.900 --> 00:50:08.700
You'll say the names — Lat, Uzza —

00:50:09.100 --> 00:50:10.766
and you'll say them loud,

00:50:11.366 --> 00:50:13.166
so every slave in Mecca hears

00:50:13.166 --> 00:50:15.100
what happens to the one who forgot himself.

00:50:17.700 --> 00:50:18.766
Say it.

00:50:19.666 --> 00:50:20.966
Say it!

00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:26.066
More weight.

00:50:26.666 --> 00:50:29.800
You will say it before the sun goes down.

00:50:39.433 --> 00:50:40.500
…Aḥad.

00:50:46.400 --> 00:50:47.966
What did you say?

00:50:51.266 --> 00:50:52.066
Aḥad.

00:50:53.466 --> 00:50:54.266
Aḥad.

00:51:35.933 --> 00:51:37.333
…Who is that?

00:51:58.966 --> 00:52:04.166
…Ibn Abi Quhafa. Abu Bakr.

00:52:18.366 --> 00:52:19.966
I have put an arrow in the ground

00:52:19.966 --> 00:52:22.666
a hundred times beside a running gazelle, Umayyah.

00:52:24.566 --> 00:52:28.533
Know that the next one does not land in the sand.

00:52:36.300 --> 00:52:38.766
You have the whole of Mecca gathered to watch the great

00:52:38.766 --> 00:52:40.866
Umayyah ibn Khalaf fight a battle

00:52:41.733 --> 00:52:44.033
against a man who cannot lift his own hand.

00:52:45.433 --> 00:52:47.833
Is this the war Quraysh is fighting now?

00:52:51.233 --> 00:52:54.366
This is my property. My sand.

00:52:54.666 --> 00:52:55.800
My business.

00:52:56.533 --> 00:52:59.100
And no concern of the house of Abu Quhafa.

00:53:09.733 --> 00:53:10.933
Your property.

00:53:13.100 --> 00:53:15.466
You've laid your property in the sun since noon

00:53:15.466 --> 00:53:16.933
with a stone on his chest.

00:53:17.033 --> 00:53:19.800
And he's been saying one name since the sun was high.

00:53:20.466 --> 00:53:22.233
You've had hours, Umayyah.

00:53:23.266 --> 00:53:25.566
Does it sound to you like he's about to stop?

00:53:25.566 --> 00:53:28.433
He will say it. If I have to—

00:53:29.466 --> 00:53:31.633
If he dies here, you have not won.

00:53:32.233 --> 00:53:34.233
You have killed good property for nothing,

00:53:34.233 --> 00:53:35.833
and handed every slave in this city

00:53:35.833 --> 00:53:37.433
a man to speak of forever.

00:53:40.300 --> 00:53:43.500
And if he lives, he lies in your sand

00:53:43.500 --> 00:53:44.500
saying that name

00:53:44.500 --> 00:53:47.133
until all of Mecca has heard it from his own mouth.

00:53:51.233 --> 00:53:53.666
You did not bring him here to break him, Umayyah.

00:53:54.300 --> 00:53:55.766
You built him a pulpit.

00:53:56.266 --> 00:53:58.233
And you carried the stone up here yourself.

00:53:59.600 --> 00:54:01.533
And what has it cost you so far?

00:54:01.633 --> 00:54:03.400
A morning. A crowd

00:54:03.400 --> 00:54:04.133
watching Umayyah

00:54:04.133 --> 00:54:06.900
ibn Khalaf wrestle a man who can't lift his own arm.

00:54:07.600 --> 00:54:09.733
They're not frightened of you out here, Umayyah.

00:54:10.033 --> 00:54:12.133
They're watching you. There's a difference,

00:54:12.133 --> 00:54:13.900
and a man as sharp as you knows it.

00:54:17.200 --> 00:54:19.900
So end it clean. Sell him to me.

00:54:20.200 --> 00:54:21.633
Name your price, Umayyah.

00:54:21.866 --> 00:54:24.133
Whatever it is — name it, and he's mine,

00:54:24.133 --> 00:54:25.166
and your morning is over,

00:54:25.166 --> 00:54:27.500
and tomorrow no one is telling this story anymore.

00:54:35.833 --> 00:54:37.333
He'll be expensive.

00:54:37.866 --> 00:54:39.400
More than he's worth.

00:54:40.400 --> 00:54:41.666
Far more.

00:54:43.200 --> 00:54:44.100
Name it.

00:54:49.466 --> 00:54:51.966
Nine ounces of gold.

00:54:56.466 --> 00:54:57.266
Done.

00:55:01.633 --> 00:55:05.400
You're a fool. If you'd argued, I'd have taken half.

00:55:09.400 --> 00:55:13.200
All this. For a broken slave who can't stand.

00:55:17.000 --> 00:55:18.700
If you'd asked ten times over,

00:55:18.700 --> 00:55:21.033
I would have paid it, and counted it cheap.

00:55:22.633 --> 00:55:24.666
You still don't know what you were holding.

00:55:30.033 --> 00:55:32.400
Take it off him. Now.

00:55:51.033 --> 00:55:53.166
It's finished. Breathe.

00:55:53.833 --> 00:55:55.300
You can stop now.

00:55:57.566 --> 00:55:58.466
…You.

00:56:21.933 --> 00:56:25.300
That's the hill-cry. Who calls from Safa?

00:56:26.800 --> 00:56:28.900
Only a man with a warning climbs that hill.

00:56:28.900 --> 00:56:31.633
A raid. An army. Come — before

00:56:31.633 --> 00:56:33.966
whatever's behind it is on us.
— Quickly.

00:56:33.966 --> 00:56:36.566
Everyone's going up. Stay close to me.

00:57:10.533 --> 00:57:14.633
Well? We left our stalls running and our doors open —

00:57:14.633 --> 00:57:16.600
what is it, then? What's coming?

00:57:19.866 --> 00:57:22.866
Say it, and we'll believe it.

00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:25.433
There's not a man on this hill

00:57:25.433 --> 00:57:27.133
who has ever caught you in a lie.

00:57:27.133 --> 00:57:31.733
Not in forty years. We ourselves named you the trustworthy.

00:57:32.166 --> 00:57:33.166
It's true.

00:57:34.266 --> 00:57:35.733
Never a false word.

00:57:36.233 --> 00:57:38.666
We named him that with our own mouths.

00:57:54.866 --> 00:57:57.166
…That's it? That's the danger

00:57:57.166 --> 00:58:00.233
you dragged the whole city up here for? The gods?

00:58:00.766 --> 00:58:01.766
He emptied the market

00:58:01.766 --> 00:58:04.333
and frightened our women up a hill — to tell us the gods

00:58:04.333 --> 00:58:06.433
our fathers lived and died by are false?

00:58:06.933 --> 00:58:10.100
We came for a warning. He gives us an insult.

00:58:13.433 --> 00:58:15.166
Ruin take you!

00:58:16.766 --> 00:58:18.833
This! This is why

00:58:18.833 --> 00:58:21.333
he's emptied your morning and pulled you up a hill

00:58:21.333 --> 00:58:22.333
by your fear!

00:58:25.366 --> 00:58:27.233
My own brother's son.

00:58:28.166 --> 00:58:30.233
Blood of Abd al-Muttalib.

00:58:31.533 --> 00:58:34.233
And he climbs Safa to spit on Lat —

00:58:34.233 --> 00:58:35.066
on Uzza —

00:58:35.066 --> 00:58:37.800
on the name of every father who built this valley

00:58:37.800 --> 00:58:38.900
with his hands!

00:58:39.233 --> 00:58:41.233
Has the sun cooked his wits?

00:58:41.533 --> 00:58:43.000
He calls you from your trade,

00:58:43.000 --> 00:58:44.600
your stalls, your work —

00:58:44.600 --> 00:58:45.066
to tell you

00:58:45.066 --> 00:58:47.466
the gods that fill your caravans are nothing?

00:58:47.633 --> 00:58:48.333
That the House

00:58:48.333 --> 00:58:51.233
all Arabia bows toward is a pile of stone?

00:58:53.433 --> 00:58:56.233
Go home! All of you with sense still in your heads —

00:58:56.233 --> 00:58:57.266
go home!

00:58:57.833 --> 00:58:59.833
There is no army behind this hill.

00:59:00.166 --> 00:59:03.133
There is only a dreamer who has shamed his own blood!

00:59:09.733 --> 00:59:12.566
Come away. Every one of you who still fears the gods —

00:59:12.566 --> 00:59:13.666
come away from him.

00:59:13.766 --> 00:59:16.066
Leave him to his hilltop and his voices.

00:59:57.266 --> 01:00:00.566
The usual measure, Harith. Same as every week.

01:00:01.933 --> 01:00:04.833
…Stock's short this week. Try another stall.

01:00:09.400 --> 01:00:10.200
Short.

01:00:12.033 --> 01:00:13.133
For me.

01:00:21.066 --> 01:00:22.166
For your kind.

01:00:23.033 --> 01:00:24.633
I've a family, Abu Bakr.

01:00:24.866 --> 01:00:27.400
A name in this market. I can't be seen

01:00:27.400 --> 01:00:28.400
filling the sack of a man

01:00:28.400 --> 01:00:29.833
who climbed that hill with him.

01:00:29.833 --> 01:00:31.266
Go. Please.

01:00:31.266 --> 01:00:33.233
Before someone sees you standing here.

01:01:03.566 --> 01:01:04.733
There he is.

01:01:04.733 --> 01:01:07.333
The man who climbs hills to frighten children.

01:01:08.233 --> 01:01:10.633
Tell me, dreamer — how does it feel

01:01:10.633 --> 01:01:13.666
to split your own clan in two and call it prophecy?

01:01:15.333 --> 01:01:16.433
To be the shame

01:01:16.433 --> 01:01:19.466
your uncle has to answer for at every gathering?

01:01:19.733 --> 01:01:22.066
Your uncle can't walk into a gathering now.

01:01:22.066 --> 01:01:24.566
You've made Abu Talib a joke in his old age.

01:01:24.933 --> 01:01:27.066
His reward, for feeding an orphan.

01:01:36.866 --> 01:01:38.933
Your gods are coming, you say.

01:01:38.933 --> 01:01:42.033
Your reckoning. I see no reckoning.

01:01:42.500 --> 01:01:43.833
Well — where is it?

01:01:44.266 --> 01:01:46.333
I see a man alone in a street

01:01:46.333 --> 01:01:49.400
whose own city walked away from him on a hilltop.

01:01:50.300 --> 01:01:53.366
You see it? Not one word.

01:01:54.000 --> 01:01:54.800
Ha!

01:01:54.900 --> 01:01:57.466
There's your prophet, people of Mecca.

01:01:57.466 --> 01:02:01.033
A man with nothing left to say.

01:02:24.133 --> 01:02:25.966
Ibn Abd al-Muttalib — forgive me.

01:02:25.966 --> 01:02:26.600
Forgive me,

01:02:26.600 --> 01:02:30.766
but I saw it myself today. With my own eyes. Near Safa.

01:02:32.000 --> 01:02:33.300
Saw what, woman?

01:02:33.400 --> 01:02:34.433
Abu Jahl.

01:02:34.733 --> 01:02:37.600
He put himself in your nephew's path in the open street.

01:02:37.600 --> 01:02:39.966
And the things he said to him — filth,

01:02:39.966 --> 01:02:41.800
my lord. Things no man should hear

01:02:41.800 --> 01:02:43.633
said to him, in front of people.

01:02:44.000 --> 01:02:46.933
He mocked him. He mocked your whole house.

01:02:47.200 --> 01:02:49.066
And your nephew answered nothing.

01:02:49.233 --> 01:02:52.033
Not one word. He only… walked away.

01:03:36.133 --> 01:03:37.333
…Hamza?

01:03:38.000 --> 01:03:40.566
You come off the hunt like a storm — what's the—

01:03:52.200 --> 01:03:54.000
That is for the street near Safa.

01:03:54.666 --> 01:03:57.100
For every filthy word you emptied onto my nephew

01:03:57.100 --> 01:03:58.400
while he said you nothing.

01:04:10.000 --> 01:04:11.633
Look at me, all of you.

01:04:12.100 --> 01:04:14.066
Every man who's been trading whispers

01:04:14.066 --> 01:04:15.700
about the house of Abd al-Muttalib —

01:04:15.700 --> 01:04:16.833
here I am.

01:04:17.866 --> 01:04:21.333
Say it to my face, or hear me say mine to yours.

01:04:24.733 --> 01:04:27.800
I follow his religion. I say what he says.

01:04:27.800 --> 01:04:30.166
The God he calls to — I call to.

01:04:39.400 --> 01:04:40.800
Say it through the whole city

01:04:40.800 --> 01:04:41.766
if you like.

01:04:42.400 --> 01:04:45.000
Hamza has crossed to his nephew's side,

01:04:45.133 --> 01:04:47.200
and he does not care who knows it.

01:04:56.833 --> 01:04:59.033
So. Any man here

01:04:59.033 --> 01:05:01.666
who thinks Abu Jahl's blood is worth the avenging —

01:05:01.666 --> 01:05:04.133
any man who believes his own sword is sharper than mine —

01:05:04.133 --> 01:05:06.200
come. Raise your hand against Muhammad

01:05:06.200 --> 01:05:07.766
while I am standing in front of you.

01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:10.433
And let us see which of you still owns a hand to raise.

01:05:21.066 --> 01:05:22.100
Leave him.

01:05:23.100 --> 01:05:25.300
Leave him! Leave him…

01:05:59.600 --> 01:06:01.233
She kissed my head this morning.

01:06:02.466 --> 01:06:04.733
Then she locked that door with her own hand.

01:06:05.333 --> 01:06:07.433
How does a mother do both in one morning?

01:06:07.500 --> 01:06:08.233
Love me enough

01:06:08.233 --> 01:06:10.033
to put me in the ground beneath her house —

01:06:10.033 --> 01:06:13.533
and not enough to sit down, one time, and ask me why?

01:06:19.333 --> 01:06:21.533
They're not fools. My uncles.

01:06:21.533 --> 01:06:22.433
The chiefs.

01:06:23.266 --> 01:06:26.566
I watched a man cut a god out of a block with a chisel.

01:06:27.400 --> 01:06:30.700
Argue its price. Promise to mend it, free, when it cracked —

01:06:30.700 --> 01:06:32.600
because he knew where every seam was.

01:06:32.933 --> 01:06:35.766
He made it. And they know it too.

01:06:36.300 --> 01:06:38.833
Every one of them knows. They've paid that man

01:06:38.833 --> 01:06:40.933
to patch their gods after a hard winter.

01:06:41.433 --> 01:06:44.133
So what is it, that a man will look straight at a thing

01:06:44.133 --> 01:06:45.900
he carved with his own hands…

01:06:46.600 --> 01:06:49.300
and put his forehead on the floor in front of it anyway?

01:06:52.833 --> 01:06:54.633
What are they so afraid of —

01:06:55.066 --> 01:06:57.466
that they would rather keep the lie, than be free of it

01:06:57.466 --> 01:06:59.733
down here, in the dark, with me?

01:07:20.466 --> 01:07:22.000
"I follow his religion."

01:07:22.533 --> 01:07:24.633
I said it to the whole of Quraysh.

01:07:24.800 --> 01:07:26.833
Shouted it off the stone of the House.

01:07:26.933 --> 01:07:29.233
Before I had ever once said it to myself.

01:07:31.700 --> 01:07:35.333
I went there for the insult. For my brother's blood,

01:07:35.800 --> 01:07:37.500
and a boy shamed in the street

01:07:37.500 --> 01:07:38.933
with no one to answer for him.

01:07:38.933 --> 01:07:41.766
My hand knew its work. My blood knew.

01:07:42.300 --> 01:07:46.033
A bow is a simple thing — you lift it, and the matter ends.

01:07:48.900 --> 01:07:52.000
But that slave. On the sand, under the stone.

01:07:52.500 --> 01:07:54.100
No one struck a blow for him.

01:07:54.100 --> 01:07:55.666
He had no bow, no name,

01:07:55.666 --> 01:07:58.500
no hand to raise. He had nothing but the word —

01:07:58.500 --> 01:07:59.833
and he would not let go of it,

01:07:59.833 --> 01:08:01.200
though it cost him everything.

01:08:01.800 --> 01:08:04.333
That is not temper. That is not blood.

01:08:04.433 --> 01:08:05.800
That is something else.

01:08:06.333 --> 01:08:08.633
Something I have never once had to find in myself.

01:08:13.600 --> 01:08:15.700
I broke a chief's head over a thing

01:08:15.700 --> 01:08:17.500
I am not sure I believe.

01:08:18.200 --> 01:08:20.366
A man should know what he carries,

01:08:20.666 --> 01:08:24.700
before he kills for it. And I do not know yet.

01:08:26.400 --> 01:08:28.600
So I will go and find out.

01:09:10.833 --> 01:09:13.033
I have never been afraid of any man in this city.

01:09:13.600 --> 01:09:14.566
Not one.

01:09:15.300 --> 01:09:17.833
But I lay in the dark last night afraid of a slave.

01:09:18.400 --> 01:09:21.300
Of what Bilal had, on that sand, that I do not.

01:09:22.400 --> 01:09:25.033
He had no sword. No name.

01:09:25.033 --> 01:09:26.566
Nothing a man could use.

01:09:26.866 --> 01:09:28.800
And they could not take the one thing from him,

01:09:28.800 --> 01:09:31.100
though they laid a mountain on his chest to try.

01:09:32.833 --> 01:09:35.600
All my life I have won by being stronger.

01:09:36.000 --> 01:09:38.166
That is the only faith a sword knows.

01:09:41.833 --> 01:09:43.266
But there is no strength in me

01:09:43.266 --> 01:09:44.500
that can do what that man did

01:09:44.500 --> 01:09:47.266
under the stone. If this is true —

01:09:47.266 --> 01:09:49.033
if it is real — then

01:09:49.033 --> 01:09:50.466
it is asking me for the one thing

01:09:50.466 --> 01:09:51.933
I have never had to find.

01:09:52.133 --> 01:09:55.000
So I have come to find out whether it is in me at all.

01:10:12.133 --> 01:10:13.800
أشهد أن لا إله إلا

01:10:13.800 --> 01:10:20.200
الله وحده لا شريك له، وأشهد أن محمدًا عبده ورسوله

01:10:37.466 --> 01:10:38.800
First it was the poor.

01:10:39.400 --> 01:10:42.500
The slaves. We told ourselves they didn't matter.

01:10:44.000 --> 01:10:45.800
Hamza struck you at the House,

01:10:45.800 --> 01:10:48.366
in front of everyone, and walked home a free man.

01:10:48.900 --> 01:10:49.733
Hamza.

01:10:50.333 --> 01:10:53.000
If he can cross over — who is safe?

01:10:53.200 --> 01:10:55.500
Whose brother is next? Whose son?

01:10:57.233 --> 01:10:59.333
The circle is closing in on us.

01:11:00.400 --> 01:11:02.300
Every month there are fewer men in this city

01:11:02.300 --> 01:11:03.633
I can be certain of.

01:11:04.533 --> 01:11:07.833
We keep reaching down — for the ones with no clan,

01:11:07.833 --> 01:11:08.633
no one to answer

01:11:08.633 --> 01:11:10.666
for them — and while our eyes are on the ground,

01:11:10.666 --> 01:11:13.400
the strong slip over to the other side behind our backs.

01:11:13.700 --> 01:11:16.100
The slave. The boy.

01:11:16.733 --> 01:11:19.533
Now the lion of the family.
— Then what is left?

01:11:19.733 --> 01:11:21.266
Hamza is beyond us.

01:11:21.266 --> 01:11:23.000
The uncle shields the nephew. We cannot

01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:24.233
touch any of them.

01:11:37.533 --> 01:11:39.233
There is still one man in this city

01:11:39.233 --> 01:11:40.966
the dreamer should be afraid of.

01:11:41.633 --> 01:11:43.800
One man strong enough to end it.

01:12:13.266 --> 01:12:16.366
Where are you going, with that face on?

01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:20.600
To finish the thing this city

01:12:20.600 --> 01:12:22.300
is too frightened to finish.

01:12:23.533 --> 01:12:25.633
One man. One sword.

01:12:25.833 --> 01:12:28.300
By tonight, Quraysh remembers what it is.

01:13:00.100 --> 01:13:00.900
Umar.

01:13:01.600 --> 01:13:03.833
You ride like a man going to collect a debt.

01:13:04.533 --> 01:13:05.933
Where to, this hour?

01:13:08.500 --> 01:13:09.366
Muhammad.

01:13:11.466 --> 01:13:14.766
…And the sword? And this fast?

01:13:16.500 --> 01:13:18.000
The sword is the debt.

01:13:18.800 --> 01:13:20.600
I'll end it myself, Nu'aym.

01:13:21.133 --> 01:13:23.933
One hand — so no other hand has to.

01:13:27.866 --> 01:13:29.966
Then put your own house in order

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:32.100
before you set all of Quraysh alight.

01:13:32.400 --> 01:13:34.300
My house is in perfect order.

01:13:35.133 --> 01:13:36.133
Is it?

01:13:37.400 --> 01:13:42.766
Then you haven't heard. Your own sister. And Sa'id,

01:13:42.866 --> 01:13:43.900
her husband.

01:13:46.933 --> 01:13:48.400
They've followed him, Umar.

01:13:49.466 --> 01:13:51.133
The thing you mean to kill a man for

01:13:51.133 --> 01:13:53.200
is already sitting at your sister's table.

01:13:55.800 --> 01:13:57.233
…Say that again.

01:14:44.333 --> 01:14:47.633
That sound. I heard it from the street.

01:14:49.200 --> 01:14:51.900
What was being recited in my own family's house?

01:14:51.900 --> 01:14:56.600
Nothing, Umar. Talk. Only talk, between me and her.

01:14:59.400 --> 01:15:03.166
Don't. Don't you stand in front of me and lie—

01:15:31.000 --> 01:15:32.166
…You're bleeding.

01:15:33.600 --> 01:15:34.733
Your face.

01:15:35.866 --> 01:15:36.666
I've—

01:15:37.500 --> 01:15:41.033
I've made you bleed. I rode here with a sword in my hand…

01:15:41.600 --> 01:15:44.333
and I have put my own sister's blood on her own floor.

01:15:44.900 --> 01:15:46.166
What have I become?

01:15:46.933 --> 01:15:49.900
This is where my anger has carried me.
— Yes.

01:15:49.933 --> 01:15:51.366
You've drawn my blood.

01:15:51.866 --> 01:15:54.033
And I will still say it to your face —

01:15:54.233 --> 01:15:58.200
the thing you came to beat out of us. We are Muslims.

01:15:58.666 --> 01:16:03.000
Sa'id and I. Now do whatever it was you came to do.

01:16:03.300 --> 01:16:04.700
It changes nothing.

01:16:11.333 --> 01:16:12.766
What were you reading?

01:16:14.033 --> 01:16:15.366
Let me see it.

01:16:16.533 --> 01:16:19.366
I want to see what is worth my sister's blood.

01:16:19.833 --> 01:16:21.733
Not with blood on your hands.

01:16:23.633 --> 01:16:27.933
Make them clean first. Then you may hold it.

01:16:49.800 --> 01:16:51.833
…What words are these?

01:16:55.100 --> 01:17:00.233
No man speaks like this. No poet I have ever heard.

01:17:02.800 --> 01:17:04.333
This was not made.

01:17:14.800 --> 01:17:15.600
Umar.

01:17:16.100 --> 01:17:19.466
I have heard him pray that Allah would strengthen

01:17:19.466 --> 01:17:21.400
this faith with one of two men.

01:17:22.266 --> 01:17:24.766
The two strongest in all of Mecca.

01:17:25.466 --> 01:17:29.133
I think, this morning, that prayer has been answered.

01:17:30.500 --> 01:17:31.766
Where is he?

01:17:33.800 --> 01:17:35.133
Where is Muhammad?

01:18:01.666 --> 01:18:02.900
It's Umar.

01:18:04.300 --> 01:18:05.533
He's armed.

01:18:13.300 --> 01:18:14.366
Open it.

01:18:17.866 --> 01:18:21.333
If he has come for good — then good, and welcome.

01:18:21.333 --> 01:18:23.333
And if he has come for anything else,

01:18:23.533 --> 01:18:26.200
his own sword will turn in his hand easily enough.

01:18:26.200 --> 01:18:27.433
I'll see to that myself.

01:18:53.333 --> 01:18:57.300
Where is he? Where is the Messenger of Allah?

01:19:16.833 --> 01:19:20.100
أشهد أن لا إله إلا الله وحده لا شريك

01:19:20.100 --> 01:19:24.566
له، وأشهد أن محمدًا عبده ورسوله

01:19:29.300 --> 01:19:38.133
الله أكبر الله أكبر الله أكبر الله أكبر الله

01:19:38.233 --> 01:19:41.300
أكبر الله أكبر

01:19:55.666 --> 01:19:56.733
Not so tight.

01:19:57.266 --> 01:19:58.833
A fist that grips out of fear

01:19:58.833 --> 01:20:00.433
is the first to drop the blade.

01:20:00.900 --> 01:20:03.800
Hold it like it already belongs to you. Loose.

01:20:04.000 --> 01:20:06.566
Awake. Ready — not afraid.

01:20:09.333 --> 01:20:10.533
It's no use.

01:20:10.600 --> 01:20:13.533
I'm not strong enough. I've never been strong enough.

01:20:17.333 --> 01:20:18.966
Strong is not the thing, Haydar.

01:20:19.500 --> 01:20:21.400
I have killed strong men who had nothing

01:20:21.400 --> 01:20:22.766
inside them but the strength.

01:20:23.200 --> 01:20:25.400
The arm is the smallest part of this.

01:20:26.033 --> 01:20:28.900
The sword only ever does what this tells it.

01:20:29.133 --> 01:20:30.233
Nothing more.

01:20:34.666 --> 01:20:37.600
Now hear me — and keep this longer than anything

01:20:37.600 --> 01:20:39.200
I ever teach you about your feet.

01:20:39.666 --> 01:20:41.200
The world will hand you a thousand

01:20:41.200 --> 01:20:42.533
reasons to draw a sword.

01:20:42.733 --> 01:20:44.966
Your pride, when a man shames you.

01:20:45.100 --> 01:20:47.000
Your temper, when your blood is up.

01:20:47.100 --> 01:20:48.633
A filthy word in the street.

01:20:49.066 --> 01:20:50.533
None of those is a reason.

01:20:51.433 --> 01:20:52.300
A man who strikes

01:20:52.300 --> 01:20:54.833
for his own anger is only a stronger kind of coward.

01:20:55.633 --> 01:20:56.566
Then when?

01:20:57.266 --> 01:20:59.900
When is it right?
— When it is for the truth.

01:21:00.233 --> 01:21:01.500
And for nothing of yourself.

01:21:02.300 --> 01:21:04.200
When your own heart is clean of it —

01:21:04.233 --> 01:21:05.733
no pride in it, no anger,

01:21:05.733 --> 01:21:07.100
nothing but what is right.

01:21:07.600 --> 01:21:09.800
The day you can tell the difference between the two —

01:21:10.300 --> 01:21:12.100
truly tell it, in the heat of the moment,

01:21:12.100 --> 01:21:13.933
with your blood screaming at you —

01:21:14.333 --> 01:21:16.566
that is the day you are ready to carry this.

01:21:25.333 --> 01:21:26.200
There.

01:21:26.933 --> 01:21:28.733
You'll carry it one day, Haydar.

01:21:29.066 --> 01:21:31.033
Better than these thin arms believe.

01:21:33.700 --> 01:21:36.800
Sooner, maybe, than any of us would wish on a boy.

01:21:53.800 --> 01:21:58.300
ELEVEN YEARS LATER

01:22:06.666 --> 01:22:11.166
BATTLE OF THE TRENCH

01:22:25.933 --> 01:22:27.966
All these days they've sat there.

01:22:28.200 --> 01:22:29.333
They can't cross the ditch,

01:22:29.333 --> 01:22:30.933
and we can't drive them off.

01:22:31.400 --> 01:22:33.400
It's the waiting that wears a man through.

01:22:33.400 --> 01:22:35.433
Not the sword. The waiting.

01:22:35.666 --> 01:22:41.333
Let them wait, then. The ditch holds. As long as it holds.

01:23:17.833 --> 01:23:19.966
So this is the army of the new faith!

01:23:20.366 --> 01:23:22.733
Men who dig a hole in the ground and crouch behind it

01:23:22.733 --> 01:23:24.800
like women barring a door against the night!

01:23:29.566 --> 01:23:32.266
I have called until my throat has gone raw.

01:23:33.700 --> 01:23:36.633
Where are your men? Where is one —

01:23:36.633 --> 01:23:37.566
just one —

01:23:37.566 --> 01:23:39.500
who will come out from behind your little ditch

01:23:39.500 --> 01:23:41.233
and stand in front of me?

01:23:43.033 --> 01:23:45.100
Is there no man among you?

01:23:54.200 --> 01:23:57.133
That garden you all weep for.

01:23:57.766 --> 01:23:59.200
That paradise.

01:24:01.866 --> 01:24:04.566
Which of you do I send to it first?

01:24:32.966 --> 01:24:35.133
Let me go to him, Messenger of Allah.

01:24:35.966 --> 01:24:37.966
Please let me go.

01:25:17.333 --> 01:25:20.433
After all my shouting, they send me one.

01:25:21.500 --> 01:25:23.600
And not a large one, at that.

01:25:30.366 --> 01:25:32.033
Before anything passes between us,

01:25:32.033 --> 01:25:33.466
Amr — hear me first.

01:25:36.366 --> 01:25:38.400
I did not come out here to kill you.

01:25:38.700 --> 01:25:41.733
I came out to call you. Leave this.

01:25:41.733 --> 01:25:44.166
Turn from it. Come to the One God,

01:25:44.166 --> 01:25:46.033
to what we follow — and live.

01:25:46.300 --> 01:25:48.366
I would far rather you lived inside the truth

01:25:48.366 --> 01:25:49.700
than died outside it.

01:25:56.466 --> 01:25:57.266
Ha!

01:25:57.433 --> 01:25:58.900
You'd preach to me?

01:25:59.400 --> 01:26:02.000
Me — with my army sitting on your ditch?

01:26:04.700 --> 01:26:08.966
No. I have sworn an oath, on my gods and on my own head.

01:26:09.866 --> 01:26:12.366
And Amr ibn Abd Wadd does not turn from an oath

01:26:12.366 --> 01:26:13.766
for a younger man's sermon.

01:26:23.100 --> 01:26:24.733
Then there is one thing more.

01:26:29.033 --> 01:26:31.900
You are mounted, and I am on foot.

01:26:32.833 --> 01:26:35.400
I will not strike a man down from under his horse.

01:26:39.266 --> 01:26:40.300
Come down.

01:26:40.900 --> 01:26:42.666
Let it be even between us.

01:26:43.266 --> 01:26:45.166
Then, whatever happens,

01:26:45.566 --> 01:26:47.533
neither of us owes the other an excuse.

01:28:48.366 --> 01:28:51.100
…What is this? You had me.

01:28:52.333 --> 01:28:54.600
You had me beaten and your blade at my throat —

01:28:54.600 --> 01:28:57.900
and you turned away. Finish it, if you mean to.

01:28:58.066 --> 01:28:59.533
Why did you stop?

01:29:05.866 --> 01:29:08.766
I had you beaten. I could have finished it then,

01:29:08.766 --> 01:29:10.933
and it would have been for Allah, and clean.

01:29:12.066 --> 01:29:13.833
But when you spat in my face,

01:29:13.933 --> 01:29:17.633
anger rose up in me. And had I killed you in that moment,

01:29:17.800 --> 01:29:19.866
I would not have been killing you for the truth.

01:29:20.366 --> 01:29:21.933
I would have been killing you for myself.

01:29:22.166 --> 01:29:25.366
For my own pride. For the insult to my own face.

01:29:29.800 --> 01:29:32.933
I will not carry a man's blood for my own anger's sake.

01:29:34.533 --> 01:29:35.633
So I waited.

01:29:37.266 --> 01:29:38.966
Until my heart was clean of it.

01:29:39.433 --> 01:29:42.833
Now I strike for Allah — and for nothing of myself.

